Hmmm seems like I can cut down the test a tad :-) File t.pl ...
<code>
use feature 'switch';
no warnings 'experimental';

$m = 'test';
given ( $m )  {
    when ('test')   {  test::Get() };
}

package test;
sub Get {
    require IO::All;
    $data = io();
}
1;
</code>
<code>
% perl t.pl 
Undefined subroutine &test::io called at t.pl line 11.
</code>
FWIW, changing the call to io()
<code>
$data = IO::All::io()
</code>
Results in a different error.
<code>
Can't call method "_package" on an undefined value at /usr/share/perl5/vendor_perl/IO/All.pm line 63.
</code>
